Month 4 — Secure AWS Web Infrastructure Project

Overview

Continued building my Secure AWS Web Infrastructure project, focusing on AWS networking, EC2 deployment, IAM permissions, S3 integration, and monitoring.

Work Completed

- Inspected existing VPCs, subnets, Internet Gateways, and route tables.
- Verified public and private subnet associations and routing configurations.
- Identified a blackhole route caused by a previously deleted NAT Gateway.
- Continued the EC2 and Nginx web server deployment.
- Configured an IAM Role for EC2 to access S3.
- Started setting up CloudWatch monitoring with an SNS notification topic.

Key Learnings

- Understood the relationship between VPCs, subnets, route tables, and Internet Gateways.
- Learned why a deleted NAT Gateway can leave a blackhole route.
- Reviewed how IAM Roles allow EC2 instances to access AWS services securely.
- Explored how CloudWatch alarms and SNS notifications support infrastructure monitoring.

Next Steps

- Complete the CloudWatch alarm configuration and test SNS notifications.
- Test the deployed website, S3 access, and security configurations.
- Troubleshoot any issues and document their root causes and solutions.
- Finalize the architecture diagram, screenshots, README, and cost-and-cleanup notes.

Outcome

Made progress toward a practical AWS infrastructure project while developing a better understanding of networking, access control, and monitoring.
